On Wednesday, October 3, 2012 8:54:13 AM UTC-7, la gleki wrote:

> I want to eat an apple    = I want that I eat an apple [a really awkward 
> lojban-style sentence]
> {mi djica lo ka citka??)  = mi djica lo nu mi/vo'a citka lo plise
>

People seem to use {nu} or {ka} a lot of times when {zu'o} would be more 
useful. At least my understanding is that {zu'o} has a {ce'u} place, as 
"giving" {lo zu'o dunda} and "receiving" {lo zu'o te dunda} are certainly 
two different activities.

